# Flutter Material 3 Default Standard

Read and follow [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) in full for every task. The most
important rules are repeated here.

- **Invisible foundation**: The design system is silent. Never place any UI
  text, label, badge or tooltip that references Material 3, AppMotion, the
  design system, or its primitives. The app's UI must contain only content that
  belongs to the product being built.
- Use Flutter's official **Material 3** (`useMaterial3: true`) with the theme in
  `lib/core/theme/app_theme.dart` for 100% of the UI.
- Take colours from `Theme.of(context).colorScheme`, text styles from
  `Theme.of(context).textTheme`, spacing from `AppSpacing`, radii from
  `AppRadii`, and motion from `context.motion` (`AppMotion`). Never hard-code
  colours, font sizes, radii, durations or magic spacing numbers.
- Use **context-aware motion & interaction** (`ContextualSwitcher`,
  `SmoothExpandable`, `TactileSurface`) only when motion communicates state,
  continuity or tactile feedback; never add decorative noise, and always respect
  `MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf(context)`. See `docs/MOTION_AND_INTERACTION.md`.
- Make **every** screen and component fully responsive using the window size
  classes in `lib/core/responsive/breakpoints.dart`, `ResponsiveBuilder`,
  `AdaptiveScaffold`, `ListDetailLayout`, `AdaptiveContentContainer`,
  `ResponsiveSliverGrid` and `FeedbackStateView`.
  Support 320 px to 2560 px wide, portrait and landscape, and 200% text scale.
- Support Android, iOS, Web, Windows, macOS and Linux. Never import `dart:io`
  in shared UI code; use `AppPlatform`.
- Use a feature-first structure: `lib/features/<feature>/presentation/...`.
  `core/` must never import from `features/`.
- Use meaningful names (Effective Dart). Extract widget classes instead of
  helper methods that return widgets. Prefer `const`.
- Document every public member with `///` comments and explain non-obvious
  logic with `//` comments.
- Add or update tests, then run `dart format .`, `flutter analyze` and
  `flutter test`. If they cannot be run, state that explicitly.
